==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|En-au-show up.ogg|a=AU}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|*|+|+|shown up}} {{tlb|en|idiomatic}}

# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To [[appear]], [[arrive]], or [[attend]], especially [[suddenly]] or [[erratically]].
#: {{ux|en|Please come on time; don't just '''show up''' whenever you feel like it.}}
#: {{ux|en|No matter how many I throw away, more copies always '''show up'''.}}
#* {{RQ:en:New York Times|author=Jim Tankersley; Katie Rogers; Lisa Friedman|quotee=Joe Biden|title=With Methane and Forest Deals, Climate Summit Offers Hope After Gloomy Start|date=2021-11-02|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2021/11/02/world/europe/climate-summit-methane-forests.html|passage=“We '''showed up'''. We '''showed up''',” Mr. Biden said at a news conference at the United Nations summit on climate change, known as COP26, in Glasgow, Scotland. “The fact that China is trying to assert, understandably, a new role in the world as a world leader, not '''showing up'''? Huh. The single most important thing that’s gotten the attention of the world is climate.”|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20220323192453/https://www.nytimes.com/2021/11/02/world/europe/climate-summit-methane-forests.html}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To be [[easily]] [[visible]]; to be [[conspicuous]].
#: {{ux|en|Stains really '''show up''' on this white tablecloth.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To make visible; to [[expose]].
#: {{ux|en|This bright light '''shows up''' the dust in the corners of the room.}}
#: {{ux|en|I bet the Jayhawk fast break could '''show up''' the Nimrod's lack of speed.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To make visible or [[expose]] [[fault]]s and [[deficiency|deficiencies]] in, usually by [[outdo]]ing, [[outperform]]ing, or [[outcompete|outcompeting]] another.
#: {{ux|en|I finished in five minutes and she '''showed''' me '''up''' by finishing in three.}}
#: {{ux|en|It '''showed''' her '''up''' in her [[true colors]].}}
#* {{RQ:Guardian|date=20 June 2014|author=Daniel Taylor|title=World Cup 2014: Uruguay sink England as Suárez makes his mark|url=http://www.theguardian.com/football/2014/jun/19/england-uruguay-match-report-group-d
|passage=His team were not outclassed but, once again, England have reminded us of their habit of being '''shown up''' as soon as they face half-decent opposition and one or two authentic category-A footballers.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20220308045114/https://www.theguardian.com/football/2014/jun/19/england-uruguay-match-report-group-d}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive|dated}} To [[produce]] an [[impression]] on [[observer]]s; to [[come off]].

====Usage notes====
* In the sense of exposing faults, the object is normally a person rather than a thing.

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|appear}} {{l|en|turn up}}

====Related terms====
* {{l|en|show off}}
* {{l|en|show out}}

